title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Fill in the form
route: /authorizations/eligibility/verify
intro: The form on the left of the Verify page, card 'Patient and service'. No header box and no instructions: bring the card in with the import row, pick a sample, or type the details. 'Check now' stays off until the four required answers look complete.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the samples under the form fill made-up members. The import reads a screenshot or a file in the browser, and its reading is simulated.
---
start s1 "Open the Verify page"
screen sc "Card 'Patient and service' with the pill 'Privacy mode on'\nImport row, the six fields, 'Check now'\nA tinted strip 'Try a sample' at the foot of the card"
click b1 "Click '← Eligibility & Benefits' (back link)"
click b2 "Click '← Back to referral RF-2040' or '← Back to case R-1042'\nShown only when the address names a referral (see 'Ways in and pre-fill')"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Referral › The full referral page"
goto g0 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › List › What the screen shows"

group gImport "Bring the card in"
  click f1 "Import row: 'Pull from EMR' (only when a record system is connected at the site in view), 'Import a file', 'Paste a screenshot'"
  process p1 "Payer and member ID filled on Apply\nA quiet line under the row: where it came from, the group and the coverage dates\n'From the sample screenshot · Group GRP-55120 · Effective 01/01/2026 to 12/31/2026'"
endgroup

group gSample "Try a sample"
  click f5 "Click a small chip in the strip 'Try a sample'\n'Cleared to bill', 'Authorization first', 'Coverage lapsed', 'Not found',\n'Not covered', 'Another plan pays first', 'Limit reached'"
  process p7 "Fills the whole form with a made-up member who ends that way\nThe chip turns green. Initials and age are remembered for the result"
endgroup

group gFields "Type the details"
  input i1 "'Payer' menu: 'Choose a payer', six payers\nUnder it, the plan type, for example 'Medicaid managed care (HMO)'"
  input i2 "'State': the only choice is 'Ohio'"
  input i3 "'Member ID'"
  input i4 "'Date of birth' as MM/DD/YYYY"
  input i5 "'Program': 'Residential 3.5', 'IOP', 'PHP', 'Detox'"
  input i6 "'Date of service' as MM/DD/YYYY, starts as 10/21/2026"
endgroup

decision q1 "Payer chosen, member ID has 4 or more letters or digits, both dates shaped MM/DD/YYYY?"
process p4 "'Check now' is off\nThe required fields carry a red star; no hint line"
process p5 "Only the shape of a date is checked, not whether it is a real day"
process p6 "'Check now' is on"
click c1 "Click 'Check now'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › The live check"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Try a sample"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Import the card or the coverage screen"

s1 --> sc
sc --> b1 --> g0
sc --> b2 --> g3
sc --> f1 --> p1 --> q1
f1 -.-> g4
sc --> f5 --> p7 --> q1
f5 -.-> g2
sc --> i1 --> i2 --> i3 --> i4 --> i5 --> i6 --> q1
q1 -->|No| p4 -.-> p5
p4 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| p6 --> c1 --> g1
